yeah they're coming out the prince is  holding the baby the royal family may  have changed beyond measure  since the births of Princes William and  Harry and so have the media who report  on them but so many of the traditions so  much of the protocol and all the theatre  of a royal birth has stayed the same the  first indication that a child has been  born will be when a member of the royal  household walks down this staircase  carrying an envelope it will contain a  notice of the birth but at this stage it  be sealed from the eyes of the world  it'll then travel by car and with a  police escort to Buckingham Palace where  the details will be revealed the car  will travel through the center of London  darkness with helicopters looking from  overhead as the world waits to find out  if the child is a prince or a princess  meanwhile at Buckingham Palace an easel  will be placed in the forecourt waiting  for the contents of the envelope it'll  be taken out of the car and framed  before being put on display by a footman  it may seem strange in the age of  Twitter but Buckingham Palace has chosen  to keep the tradition of the easel it  maintains a sense of occasion about the  birth it's the same one that was used to  announce the arrival of Prince William  and it's the way the world is going to  discover whether the latest member of  the royal family is male or female as  news of the baby's arrival spreads the  story of the future king or queen begins  but his or her birth will be heralded in  much the same way as the last royal  generation
 

